-- id: exp6849-typed-program-isomorphic-authority-audit
-  title: Independent typed-program isomorphic authority audit
-  track: verification
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 240
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.599
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6849_typed_program_isomorphic_authority_audit.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6848-v599-method-change-evidence-contract
-      artifact_field: v599_evidence_contract_ready_score
-      op: '=='
-      value: 1
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6836 built the typed obligation program, but Exp6847 found duplicated candidate identities and
-    recomputed compile parity as false. LLMs Gaming Verifiers (arXiv:2604.15149) shows that an
-    extensional verifier can accept shortcuts that fail under isomorphic perturbation. This task
-    rebuilds authority before any model score is interpreted. It invokes no LLM.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/research-references.md, V599 Planner Refresh
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6836_typed_obligation_program_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6847_v598_independent_capstone.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6848_v599_method_change_evidence_contract.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/constraint_obligation_automaton.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py
-
-    TASK:
-    Implement a fresh typed-program reducer and sanitized fixed-candidate fixture. Require unique
-    semantic and row identities. Recompile every view and test semantics-preserving transformations,
-    duplicate removal, and exact negative controls. The exact checker is authority.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require v599_evidence_contract_ready_score=1, readable Exp6836 raw fixture
-       material, and the Exp6847 discrepancy rows. Write
-       complete_blocked_typed_program_isomorphic_authority_audit with gate_check_summary on failure.
-    1. Add REQ-CONSTRAINT-6849 and testable scenarios before implementation. Cover duplicate IDs,
-       semantic aliasing, atom omission, impossible programs, row collision, and reducer mutation.
-    2. Do not import Exp6836's reducer. Parse its raw typed programs and construct new unique
-       candidate, pair, atom, view, transform, and row identifiers.
-    3. Compile the exact energy, satisfaction predicate, memory guard, ARC guard, and diagnostic from
-       one typed source. Compare every view on every base and perturbed row.
-    4. Apply identifier permutations, atom renames, label swaps, row reorderings, surface paraphrases,
-       duplicate removal, and one-atom semantic mutations. Isomorphic rows must preserve labels;
-       semantic mutations must not.
-    5. Freeze a sanitized candidate-pair manifest for Exp6851. Store raw sequence inputs. Store no
-       model scores and do not infer token equality without tokenizer receipts.
-    6. Set typed_program_authority_ready_score and isomorphic_fixture_ready_score to 1 only when all
-       exact parity, uniqueness, invariance, and mutation gates pass.
-    7. Run focused tests, ruff, OpenSpec coverage, adversarial verification, artifact convention
-       audit, mutation tests, verdict-row consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles; preconditions_checked;
-       inference_substrate (deterministic CPU exact compilation); duration_s; source_artifact_hashes;
-       random_seed; reproducibility_checksum; rows (one typed view, candidate, and transform);
-       fresh_reducer_manifest; candidate_identity_manifest; collision_witnesses;
-       compiled_view_parity_rows; isomorphic_transform_manifest; semantic_mutation_rows;
-       duplicate_removal_results; sanitized_candidate_pair_manifest;
-       authority_audit_complete_score; typed_program_authority_ready_score (exact field consumed by
-       Exp6851); isomorphic_fixture_ready_score (exact field consumed by Exp6851);
-       gate_check_summary (failed check and observed value for any blocked verdict);
-       verifier_is_oracle (false, exact checkers supply external truth); verdict_class (positive |
-       circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and
-       prefixed complete_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6849_typed_program_isomorphic_authority_audit.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
-  prior_failures:
-    - experiment_id: exp6836-typed-obligation-program-fixture
-      verdict: complete_null_typed_obligation_program_fixture_ready_no_model_scores
-      addressed_by: 'Exp6847 independently rejected the producer readiness fields. This attempt uses a fresh reducer, unique identities, duplicate removal, and isomorphic invariance before it emits authority readiness.'
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
-    - experiment_id: exp6487-representation-integrity-audit
-      verdict: 'disqualified: candidate_identifier_length,candidate_identity,row_order_modulo_pair,token_length_unavailable_from_raw_rows,candidate_length_unavailable_from_raw_rows,prompt_length_unavailable_from_raw_rows'
-      addressed_by: 'The sanitized fixture records unique identities and raw candidate inputs before scoring. This task tests identifier, label, order, surface, and semantic transforms with exact labels.'
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
